  "comments": "NOTE: Kremnica and Leningrad Mint can be distinguished by some details:<br />\r\nOn coins from Kremnica Mint, the left point of the star points between A and T of PATRIA<br />\r\nOn coins from Leningrad Mint, the left point of the star points on the right leg of the A<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/58eee43959516.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/58eee43959516.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"150\" /></a><br /><br />\r\nSome minor variations in lettering and design between 1971/1972 and 2001-date coin:<br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/58017249f2707.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/58017249f2707.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"229\" /></a><br /><br />\r\n1972 coins started circulating on the 90&#039;s; that is the reason why no coins were minted between 1972-2001.<br /><br />\r\n<a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5beecb9f32b9c.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5beecb9f32b9c.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"199\" height=\"94\" /></a><a href=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/5beecbb5a9b56.jpg\"><img src=\"https://en.numista.com/catalogue/images/miniatures/5beecbb5a9b56.jpg\" alt=\"\" width=\"200\" height=\"88\" /></a><br />\r\n2002 variants: High date on left, low date on right, distance from date to edge is different<br />\r\n(source: pictures by adanieluy).<br /><br />\r\nOn 2016 legend was changed from &quot;PATRIA Y LIBERTAD&quot; to &quot;PATRIA O MUERTE&quot;, this legend have been changed on 1 and 2 centavos coins on 1983, and on 20 and 40 centavos on 1982, but remained unchanged on 5 centavos value. 2016 coins are not still listed on Krause, this is the reason they show &quot;NO KM#&quot; in years comments, you can see new version on its own page (see link below).",
